  "description": "A parametric WALL CABINET on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE UPPER HALF OF THE KITCHEN COUNTER, and deliberately its twin: segment-hosted, Exact fit by default, the same Auto unit division at 600 mm, the same bounded loop building the fronts. Drop both on the same wall and the runs line up, unit for unit, because they divide the same length by the same rule.\n\nMOUNTED BY UNDERSIDE HEIGHT, not by floor height, because that is the dimension that matters — and the published \"Gap over a 0.9 m worktop\" does the subtraction most people do in their head and get wrong. Under 450 mm and the kettle does not fit.\n\nTHE PELMET IS A REAL PIECE, a shallow strip under the front edge where the lighting goes. It is off by default in depth terms only — set it to zero and it disappears without a second switch fighting the first.",
